<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">George II of Greece</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1890">1890</a>–<a href="/years/1947">1947</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">George II of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a> was king from 1922 to 1924 and again from 1935 to 1947. He was exiled when the Second Hellenic Republic was proclaimed and returned after a disputed plebiscite in 1935. He backed the Metaxas <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dictatorship">dictatorship</a> from 1936 and led the government in exile after the German invasion of 1941, returning to Greece in 1946.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/george-ii-of-greece.jpg" alt="George II of Greece" width="320" height="441" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: United States Office of War Information, Overseas Picture Division, Washington Division. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Georgeiiofgreece.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>A plebiscite restored <b>George II</b> in 1935, but in 1936 he allowed Ioannis Metaxas to establish a dictatorship.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-greece">Kingdom of Greece · Governance &amp; Law</a></li><li><blockquote>After Germany invaded Greece in April 1941, General Georgios Tsolakoglou surrendered the army and was installed as prime minister of a collaborationist government in Athens, while <b>King George II</b> and the legitimate government fled to Egypt.</blockquote><a href="/state/hellenic-state-1941-1944">Hellenic State (1941-1944)</a></li><li><blockquote>In October 1935 General Georgios Kondylis seized power, and a rigged plebiscite restored the monarchy, bringing back <b>George II</b>.</blockquote><a href="/state/second-hellenic-republic">Second Hellenic Republic</a></li></ul></section>
